{{!-- templates/v2/apps/homebrew-settings.hbs — AppV2 (no <form> wrapper) --}}
<section class="uesrpg-settings">
<fieldset>
  <legend>Movement</legend>

  <div class="form-group">
    <label>Speed Formula: SB + AB (Homebrew)</label>
    <input type="checkbox" name="homebrew.speedFormulaSBAB" {{checked homebrewSpeedFormulaSBAB}}>
    <p class="notes">
      When enabled, base Speed is computed as <strong>SB + AB + bonus</strong> (Homebrew)
      instead of the RAW formula <strong>SB + (2 × AB) + bonus</strong>.
      Applies to all Characters and NPCs. <em>Requires a reload to apply consistently.</em>
    </p>
  </div>
</fieldset>

<fieldset>
  <legend>Combat — Reach &amp; Length (Harnmaster-inspired)</legend>

  <div class="form-group">
    <label>Enable Reach &amp; Length Overhaul</label>
    <input type="checkbox" name="homebrew.reachLength.enabled" {{checked homebrew.reachLengthEnabled}}>
    <p class="notes">
      Unlocks per-weapon <strong>Length (LNG)</strong> and homebrew reach overrides, the
      <strong>In Close</strong> Token HUD condition, and Length Penalty TN automation.
      <em>Requires a reload to apply consistently.</em>
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="form-group">
    <label>Reach Model</label>
    <select name="homebrew.reachLength.reachModel" {{#unless homebrew.reachLengthEnabled}}disabled{{/unless}}>
      <option value="classic" {{#if (eq homebrew.reachLengthModel "classic")}}selected{{/if}}>Classic (Min + Max Reach)</option>
      <option value="simplified" {{#if (eq homebrew.reachLengthModel "simplified")}}selected{{/if}}>Simplified (Max Reach Only)</option>
    </select>
    <p class="notes">
      <strong>Classic:</strong> Weapons have both a minimum and maximum reach (polearms cannot attack adjacent).
      <strong>Simplified:</strong> Only maximum reach is used (no minimum reach gating).
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="form-group">
    <p class="notes">
      When enabled: Length Penalty automation (ΔL×5 on parry/counter), the <strong>In Close</strong>
      Token HUD condition with pairwise tracking, and auto-prune when tokens move beyond 1 m are all
      active. The only option is which reach model to use.
    </p>
  </div>
</fieldset>

<fieldset>
  <legend>Combat — Engagement &amp; Flanking</legend>

  <div class="form-group">
    <label>Enable Engagement &amp; Flanking</label>
    <input type="checkbox" name="homebrew.engagementFlanking.enabled" {{checked homebrew.engagementFlankingEnabled}}>
    <p class="notes">
      Auto-computes <strong>Flanked (X)</strong> from nearby threats, defensive skill, and ally support from shared threatened foes.
      Melee attacks and melee maneuvers against that target gain <strong>+5 TN per Flanked point</strong>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="form-group">
    <label>Only In Combat</label>
    <input type="checkbox" name="homebrew.engagementFlanking.onlyInCombat" {{checked homebrew.engagementFlankingOnlyInCombat}}>
    <p class="notes">
      Restricts Flanked automation to active combats only (<code>game.combat.started</code>).
    </p>
  </div>

</fieldset>

<footer class="sheet-footer flexrow">
  <button type="submit" class="save"><i class="fas fa-save"></i> Save</button>
</footer>
</section>
